  "note": "Decision-faithful replay of lua_momentum on the four checked-in 1h windows (docs/reports/data/mean-reversion-gate). Not a kernel backtest: those tapes have book+round events and no resolution, so a hold is marked at the last two-sided mid only when that mid is >=0.90 (pays 1) or <=0.10 (pays 0); every other hold is an unresolved last-bid mark, not a settlement. Maker entry: the first confirming best bid rests until a later ask crosses it. Exits re-arm the entry rule, so the with-exits arm trades more than once per token. Giveback is peak fee-net unrealized USD minus realized USD, floored at 0; armed_giveback counts only positions whose peak net PnL reached +20%. realistic subtracts 0.07*p*(1-p) on sells; polysim_fee0 does not. A redemption itself is not a taker fill. max_dd is the stitched equity curve."
